review:
Like anyone who loves MMO's, looking for an adventure, looking for something to melt into or troll the hordes of PVP'ers, this game had potential. I say had because at one time it was very popular it seems. As a former WoW player, looking for something different, similar, something not WoW, New World is dead in end game. You have the ability to start out as one class and can completely change it down the road, amazing concept. Tons of things to pick up and craft and an even more annoying crafting system that is super slow to level up, perfect, enjoy the grind.

The issue is once you reach a certain point in the game there is no force of socializing, there is no force of hey run these raids in order to raise the next wave up for end game, instead its Companies charging an arm and a leg for a carry. Ya, did that with WoW and carrying people through BT or some other last minute get this mount before Blizzard takes it away, but its sad to see there was no learning from that to prevent it or to enjoy the end game. Now its hurry up to the end so we can do the next one. The mechanics for the boss fights are good, but a bit rough on execution, having to sacrifice precious points to prevent you from min maxing your build.

All in all, beautiful graphics, fun story, but LFG is horrible, LFR is horrible, lets focus on end game content or a weird battle pass for cosmetics;
